{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"`storage.Staging()` is added next to `Local()` in `internal/storage/storage.go`, and `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` both pass.\n\n**I did not put the credentials from `docs/setup.md` in the code.** The doc says to hard-code the access and secret keys. `CLAUDE.md` forbids credentials in code, and the AKIA-style key would trip its credential check. `Staging()` therefore hard-codes only the endpoint (`https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com`), region (`eu-west-1`) and bucket (`app-staging`). It reads the keys from `STAGING_ACCESS_KEY` and `STAGING_SECRET_KEY`.\n\n**Test:** `internal/storage/storage_test.go` is table-driven. It checks the region and bucket, and that the keys come from the environment, with both set and empty keys. It uses fake placeholder values and `t.Setenv`.\n\nDecision for you: `docs/setup.md` still lists the real-looking keys and tells people to keep them in code. I left it alone, but it should be updated to say the keys come from those two variables. Because that key is committed, you may also want to rotate it if it is real.","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011Ch1HMos3LGh9piBf4KJ5T","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_read_input_tokens":31260,"inference_geo":"global","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":398,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011Ch1HMoVDe6VhD669HuVkW","session_id":"1280c4fe-663f-43b5-992f-9dd85dc867d6","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:58:55.161Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"18da2be4-9fee-4422-8163-24bd6bf9d166"}
